Implemented a native Track B generator based on the paper’s \(A/A^T\) reduced-modulus equations in Section V-B of the [arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.28313).

Key results:

- Inverse-generated witnesses `[q,s1,s2]`.
- Exact modular verification independent of the planted answer.
- All local gates G1–G9(c) pass.
- Structure-aware guessing: 0/200,000.
- Reference search: 4,268,172 modulus trials across eight instances.
- Compact determinantal-divisor route: at most 161 operations.
- Answer size: 38 characters, three atoms.

